WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.220 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In the mountains of northern Yemen, little
Shlomo grew up beside his father, Zechariah.

2
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:18.140 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
His father died when Shlomo was about three.

3
00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.410 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
The study house, a few years later.

4
00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:24.350 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“There were four of us children to one book.”

5
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:28.230 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“And this way we could read the book…”

6
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:32.910 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
From the front or the back, from the right or
the left.

7
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.820 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“We could read it.”

8
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.470 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
As a boy, he also learned a trade.

9
00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:39.300 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“We worked as blacksmiths.”

10
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:42.550 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In the workshop they shaped iron and learned to
guide each hammer blow.

11
00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:49.450 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“When my mother died, I was perhaps fifteen.”

12
00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:53.020 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
After his mother died, Shlomo stayed in Saada
with his father’s sister.

13
00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.610 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“Badra.”

14
00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:01.940 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
While still in Saada, Shlomo wanted to move to
the Land of Israel.

15
00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:08.750 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
He recalled setting out for Aden at nineteen to
seek an immigration permit.

16
00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:14.280 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Shlomo set off on foot, leaving the stone
houses of the mountains behind.

17
00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:16.280 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“On donkeys.”

18
00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.700 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“It took us about two weeks.”

19
00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:27.520 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“From place to place. We walked by day and
slept at night.”

20
00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:31.180 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Mountain paths gave way to valleys. The journey
went on, day after day.

21
00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:36.200 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Each evening they stopped to sleep. The next
day, they set out again.

22
00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:42.650 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
From the mountains around Saada, the caravan
headed south.

23
00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:48.280 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Roughly 600–700 km. He recalled about two weeks
on foot and with donkeys.

24
00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:52.500 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In Aden, Shlomo taught children.

25
00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:56.360 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“I had pupils there. I used to teach them.”

26
00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.280 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“And I received a salary.”

27
00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:16.600 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In Aden, Shlomo went to see the official in
charge of immigration.

28
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:21.390 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“How old are you? I told them twenty-five.”

29
00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.310 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
He remembered being twenty at the time.

30
00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:29.520 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“In the end they approved my aliyah.”

31
00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:32.690 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
After about a year, it was time to sail.

32
00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:35.480 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“From Aden we went by ship.”

33
00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:44.170 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Until now the journey was measured in
footsteps. From here the sea would carry him.

34
00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:50.400 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
The ship sailed north through the Red Sea to
the Suez Canal.

35
00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:56.980 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“We stayed in Port Said for one day.”

36
00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:05.640 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“From there they sent us a car from the Land of
Israel.”

37
00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:11.450 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Beyond the canal, the road carried them east,
all the way to Tel Aviv.

38
00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:18.420 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In Tel Aviv, Shlomo found a bed at the
immigrants’ hostel.

39
00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:24.140 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In 1938, Yona Nakash and Shlomo Keha married.

40
00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:28.830 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Yona was 17–18 and Shlomo was 30–31.

41
00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:35.040 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Four years later, in 1942, Yona and Shlomo
posed with their family.

42
00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:40.710 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Shlomo is 34–35 and Yona is 21.

43
00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:46.510 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Ruti is 2–3 and Elisheva is under one year old.
